<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 1.671 mln bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 1.671 mln bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's cotton output had reached 1.671 million 375-lb bales by October 15 in the 1996/97 (July-June) crop year, the Pakistan Cotton Ginners Association said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Aijazuddin Ghauri, secretary of the association, could not give comparative figures for last year because the association had not then been collecting fortnightly data.</p>
<p>Ghauri said textile mills had purchased 1.182 million bales of the new crop and the rest was at ginneries. Officials have estimated the 1996/97 crop at 9.2 to 9.5 million bales, compared to 9.96 million in 1995/96. -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
